      "role": "user",
      "content": "so you're saying the \"balanced approach\" is actually more about validating the identity part? because it feels like you're saying that the biological view is somehow potentially harmful or \"invalidating\" to kids. isn't there also a valid argument that prioritizing feelings over physical reality could be confusing or even detrimental to a child's understanding of the world? i'm just trying to understand why one way is considered the \"most helpful\" path.",
